[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1660","stub":{"id":"1660","section":"Shohola Falls Park to Mouth (at Delaware R.)","altname":"","river":"Shohola Creek","difficulty":"ItoIV","states":["USA-PEN"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"104","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"108950","location":{"latitude":"41.390478","longitude":"-74.968969"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"114185","location":{"latitude":"41.472043","longitude":"-74.912788"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"9.5","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"101250134","title":null,"post_date":"2013-04-23 04:00:00+00","detail":"Ran the Shohola from waterfall down thru the second box canyon on 4/21/13. Level was 2.36. Some, but tolerable, scraping through the flats, but wouldn't want to run it much lower. While the beams from the broken construction bridge (October 2011-aftermath of Hurricane Irene) appear to be removed completely there is still some wood to be on the look out for in the class 3 rapid after the top box; lots of wood in the flat section (about 3 non negotiable portages); and there is wood in the second box canyon before the take out- recommend scouting it, not sure how it will play out at different levels.","user":{"name":"Carin Tinney"}}],"photos":[{"id":"884582","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"887290","description":"2.25 on Bushkill Gauge / 42cfs on Little Bushkill Gauge","caption":"Shahola Falls - Left Line","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Adam Nawrot","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/884582","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/884582"}},{"id":"878765","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879201","description":"Upper Shohola Gorge at relatively high flow = Schweet","caption":"Upper Gorge, Shohola Creek","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Bob North","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/878765","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/878765"}},{"id":"9424","ext":"gif","post_id":"4445","description":"This map shows the relation ship of the rain gauge to the Shohola watershed.","caption":"Raingauge Map for Shohola Cr.","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Stephen Strange","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/9424","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/9424"}},{"id":"9710","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4445","description":"This is a view upstream from near the end of the first gorge. It begins at the base of the falls and goes for about 1/4-1/2 a mile.","caption":"Upper box on Shohola Creek","poi_name":"Upper Box","subject":"","author":"Stephen Strange","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/9710","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/9710"}},{"id":"9711","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4445","description":"This is an easy put-in at the end of the first gorge. ","caption":"Put-In at the end of the first gorge","poi_name":"","subject":"Matt Sasson","author":"Stephen Strange","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/9711","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/9711"}},{"id":"13918","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8480","description":"","caption":"Left line","poi_name":"Shohola falls","subject":"Jared seiler","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13918","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13918"}},{"id":"13213","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4446","description":"","caption":"Thumbnail of Vertical Line at Shohola Falls","poi_name":"Shohola Falls","subject":"Grizzle shwizzlemon   ","author":"shmiegle","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13213","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13213"}},{"id":"9716","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4445","description":"There is some surf on this run, as on any ledgy run.","caption":"Surf on the Shohola","poi_name":"","subject":"Matt Sasson","author":"Stephen Strange","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/9716","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/9716"}},{"id":"13178","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4447","description":"This is a low level on Shohola. This top canyon is runnable, but the rest of the run (though you could probably get down it)is too low.","caption":"The First \"Box Canyon\"","poi_name":"Under the bridge","subject":"","author":"Stephen Strange","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13178","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13178"}},{"id":"9893","ext":"asf","post_id":"6054","description":"","caption":"Sholola slide","poi_name":"Sholola Falls (left line)","subject":"Matt Walker","author":"Jeff","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/9893","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/9893"}},{"id":"13211","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8481","description":"","caption":"Shohola vertical line","poi_name":"Shohola Falls","subject":"Grizzle shwizzlemon","author":"shmiegle","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13211","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13211"}},{"id":"9709","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4445","description":"I know of three lines down this. Straight down the bouncy slide on the left, down a series of increasingly  larger ledges on the right, and down the right until the last drop, then cutting left for the finish.","caption":"Shohola Falls","poi_name":"Shohola Falls","subject":"","author":"Stephen Strange","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/9709","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/9709"}}],"detail":{"id":"1660","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"The Shohola is an odd river. It begins with a runnable (with multiple lines) 50ft waterfall/cascade. Then goes through a box canyon with class III to IV water for most of it's 1/2 mile length. Then, after another 1/2 mile or so of good whitewater, it goes through a very flat period where relatively slow moving flatwater paddling is interspersed with a ledge occasionally. Finally, it finishes with some good slides and another box canyon with a good drop at it's entrance. The scenery is beautiful at times and nice the rest of the time. It's a fun creek, but if your plan is to run the whole thing, it can be a longish day, so get on early in the winter, when the days are short.\n\nIt can pick up wood (and ice in winter), so keep your eyes ahead and scout the box canyons from the rim (if possible) before entering. This is easy on the first one (there's a trail along the rim on river right), and not too difficult from river right on the second one. Hiking out from the middle of this run if someone gets hurt could be tedious, look at the map before you get on.\n\nNowadays most people only run the top box. It's the most bang for your buck. Just carry up the trail on river right and repeat offend. (It takes about 15 minutes down the river and about 15-20 minutes up the trail to complete a lap, depending on how fast you paddle and/or hike.)\n\nThere is also a lot of private land around here so be careful when scouting. Once a group of us was paddling on a rare, warm sunny day in April and we came around a bend to find a man lying naked on his lawn, sunning himself. He was a little surprised to see 7 of us paddle by.\n\nThere is now an online gauge on the Shohola itself, at Knealing Rd., above the last gorge, so that's the gauge to use now.\n\nThe gauge on the Bush Kill at Shoemaker used to be the main online indicator for this run.  It should be over 2.5', and gives a good correlation, but the Shohola drains a large swampy area above the lake and will generally stay up longer than The Bushkill. Sometimes for many days longer. If it's at 2.4 and dropping slowly, the Shohola will most likely still be up.","averageGradient":"65","maxGradient":"220","length":"9.4","correlations":[{"reachID":"1660","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"140","beginMediumRunnable":"350","beginHighRunnable":"1000","endHighRunnable":"1600"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"Shohola Creek near Walker Lake, PA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"01432495","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"104","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"3.92","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"41.45","longitude":"-74.9216667"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/01432495","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/01432495/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExpl